**** Sets or hashsets in java are special concepts which are used to store data with mre tha one variable
     but the values should not contain duplicates.

*** to access the java set we need to import java.util.set or import java.util.*;

**** In the sets also we can add the add the values using the add() methode

**** set prints the value without any specific order, It doesn't have indexing option

      Example :  [10,20,30] --> printing the values as 20 -> 30 -> 10
      if we by mistake add any duplicate values it will not print those values


Methods that are used in the set or Hashset are :

        - add(E e)
        Adds the specified element to the set if it's not already present.
        - remove(Object o)
        Removes the specified element if it exists in the set.
        - contains(Object o)
        Checks if the set contains the given element.
        - isEmpty()
        Returns true if the set contains no elements.
        - size()
        Returns the number of elements in the set.
        - clear()
        Removes all elements from the set.
        - iterator()
        Returns an iterator over the elements.







